{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98910","id":2166234935,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6BHh83","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98910","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98910.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98910.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98910","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98910/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98910/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98910/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/e69a0c7d60ea4b0401558da4b48bdc2fe1e87edd","number":98910,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Force `RDD::id` to be always `uint64_t`","user":{"login":"darksylinc","id":3395130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTUxMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3395130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc","html_url":"https://github.com/darksylinc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"On Vulkan, some handles are meant to always be u64, even on 32-bit architectures such as arm32.\r\n\r\nFixes #98654\r\n\r\n# Testing methodology\r\n\r\nTesting this is hard, because most platforms Godot is meant to be run on are already 64-bit.\r\nEffectively this only affects arm32.\r\n\r\nMy particular worry is what if at some point Godot does the following? (or similar)\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nvoid * ptr = (void *)buffer.id; // Ooops! This is downgraded from 64 to 32 bit\r\nbuffer.id = (size_t)ptr;\r\n```\r\n\r\nMore bizarre stuff such as memcpy could be happening.\r\n\r\nTo check for this very particular scenario I was afraid of, I devised a much larger patch I'm including here:\r\n\r\n[arch32_test.patch.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17653996/arch32_test.patch.zip)\r\n\r\nWhich changes RenderingDeviceDriver::id to private and is a RenderingDeviceDriver::id[3]; where I store the value in id[1].\r\n\r\nThis way, if Godot were to make such horrible type punning (or other dangerous raw manipulation), the value would be lost even on an x64 machine.\r\n\r\nI tested this patch, and Godot ran fine. I tested 3 different projects, but not thoroughly.\r\n\r\nSo far this change appears to be harmless. But I can never be 100% certain. Type punning Vulkan & D3D12 handles as RenderingDeviceDriver::id was not the best idea to begin with. But it is what we have.\r\n\r\nHopefully CI will agree.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","description":"","color":"ffee88"